module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.CoverLifting
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.ComparisonSurjectivity

/-!
# Over an object in the image of the functor of sites, the pullback is the image of the unit

Let `F : C ⥤ D` be a functor of sites, `φ : S ⟶ F.op ⋙ R` a morphism of presheaves of rings and
`ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj Q` a morphism of presheaves of modules, with adjoint transpose
`ψ^♯ : (pullback φ).obj P ⟶ Q`.  Mathlib defines `PresheafOfModules.pullback` as a partial left
adjoint of the pushforward and gives no description of its sections, so the only description of
the image of `ψ^♯` available is the *generation* half,
`PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule`: over an object `Y` of `D` the
image of `ψ^♯` is the `R(Y)`-submodule generated by the restrictions along all `F(X) ⟶ Y` of the
image of `ψ`.

This file collapses that generated submodule to a plain image, over the objects `Y` which are of
the form `F(X₀)`:

* a generator over `F(X₀)` is a restriction along a morphism `F(X₀) ⟶ F(X)`, hence — when `F` is
  **full** — along `F(k)` for some `k : X₀ ⟶ X`, and the naturality of `ψ` turns such a
  restriction into a value of `ψ` over `X₀` again;
* so the image of `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)` is the `R(F X₀)`-submodule *spanned* by the image of `ψ` over
  `X₀`, and that span is the image itself as soon as `φ.app X₀` is **surjective**, because the
  image of a semilinear map along a surjection is a module over the target ring.

The consequence is the implication the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JN] uses when it calls the
surjectivity of the comparison map `c_f : f^* F_{T'} ⟶ F_T` and the surjectivity of the `f`-map
`F_{T'} ⟶ f_* F_T` equivalent: `surjective_appₛₗ_of_surjective_homEquivSymm_app` objectwise and
`isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_homEquivSymm` for a pair of Grothendieck topologies.
The comparison for crystalline thickenings,
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.range_moduleComparison_app`, gives the opposite
inclusion only.

## Main results

* `PresheafOfModules.pushforwardGenerators_subset_range_appₛₗ` — for a **full** `F`, every
  generator of the image of `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)` is already a value of `ψ` over `X₀`.
* `PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_range_appₛₗ` — **the image of `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)` is
  the image of `ψ` over `X₀`**, for a full `F` and a `φ.app X₀` surjective on sections.
* `PresheafOfModules.exists_appₛₗ_eq_homEquivSymm_app` — the same statement read on elements: every
  value of `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)` is a value of `ψ` over `X₀`.
* `PresheafOfModules.surjective_appₛₗ_of_surjective_homEquivSymm_app` and
  `PresheafOfModules.surjective_homEquivSymm_app_of_surjective_appₛₗ` — **the two surjectivities
  are equivalent**, the second direction with no hypothesis at all.
* `PresheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_homEquivSymm` — **the local form**:
  for topologies `J` on `C` and `K` on `D` with `F` cocontinuous, a `K`-locally surjective `ψ^♯`
  forces a `J`-locally surjective `ψ`.

## What is and is not proved

The hypotheses, exactly.

* `pushforwardGenerators_subset_range_appₛₗ` assumes `[F.Full]` and nothing else.  Fullness is
  genuinely needed and is not a convenience: the generators of the image of `ψ^♯` over an object
  `Y` are the restrictions along *arbitrary* morphisms `F(X) ⟶ Y`, and such a restriction is a
  value of `ψ` over `Y` again only when the morphism itself comes from `C`.
* `range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_range_appₛₗ` and its corollaries assume in addition that
  `φ.app X₀ : S(X₀) ⟶ R(F X₀)` is surjective on sections.  That hypothesis is as necessary here as
  in `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Presheaf.exists_apply_eq_transpose_apply`; the counterexample
  without it is the one recorded in the implementation notes of
  `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.PullbackSectionsBaseChange` (`S` the constant
  presheaf `ℤ`, `R` the constant presheaf `ℚ`, `P = S`, `Q = R`, `ψ` the inclusion: the transpose
  is the identity of `ℚ ⊗_ℤ ℤ = ℚ`, which is surjective, while `ψ` is not).
* `isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_homEquivSymm` assumes `[F.Full]`,
  `[F.IsCocontinuous J K]` and surjectivity of `φ` on sections over **every** object.  No
  hypothesis on `P`, on `Q` or on the topologies is used; in particular neither presheaf of modules
  need be a sheaf, and no quasi-coherence, flatness or presentation enters.

What is **not** proved.

* **No description of the sections of `PresheafOfModules.pullback` is produced here.**  This file
  computes an *image*, not a module: it says which sections of `Q` are hit by `ψ^♯`, and says
  nothing about the kernel.  The tensor-product descriptions of the sections themselves live
  elsewhere in this library and are not restated:
  `Stacks.PullbackColimit.pullbackObjIso` identifies the sections of the pullback over `U` with a
  colimit of base changes over `CostructuredArrow F.op U` for an arbitrary `F`,
  `Stacks.NoncommChangeOfRings.Presheaf.pullbackObjIso` identifies them with a single base change
  when `F` is the identity, and `Stacks.PullbackEquivalence.pullbackObjIsoBaseChange` does so when
  `F` is fully faithful and `U` is isomorphic to an `F(V₀)`.  All three are *presheaf*-level; the
  corresponding statement for `SheafOfModules.pullback` is false, the sheaf pullback being the
  sheafification of the presheaf one.
* The results here are strictly more general than
  `Stacks.PullbackEquivalence.surjective_app_of_surjective_comparison`, which proves the objectwise
  implication through the colimit model and therefore needs `F` **faithful** as well as full, the
  presheaves of rings to be valued in `CommRingCat`, and `C` and `D` to be small.  None of that is
  needed for an image: only fullness and the surjectivity of the ring map.  That module records the
  local form as missing, "for a general `F` the comparison map and the map it transposes live on
  different sites, so transporting local surjectivity needs the equivalence to be continuous for
  the two topologies"; `isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_homEquivSymm` is that step, with
  cocontinuity of `F` as the hypothesis which makes it work.
* Nothing here carries a `@[stacks]` attribute.  Neither the collapse nor the surjectivity transfer
  is tagged content of the source; both are auxiliaries used in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JN].

## Implementation notes

The generation half, `PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule`, lives in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.ComparisonSurjectivity`, which is why a file
of general module theory imports a module of the crystalline tree: re-deriving the generated
sub-presheaf of modules here would declare a second `PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule`, and two
modules declaring one fully qualified name with different statements cannot be imported together.
The route through `Stacks.PullbackColimit` is unavailable for the same reason in reverse — that
module and `ComparisonSurjectivity` both declare `PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_comp_apply` and its
companions — and is in any case not needed, the colimit model being a description of the sections
and this file needing only an image.

The surjectivity of `φ.app X₀` is used through `RingHomSurjective`, which is what makes
`LinearMap.range (appₛₗ φ ψ X₀)` a submodule over the *target* ring `R(F X₀)` rather than merely an
additive subgroup; the collapse of the span is then `Submodule.span_le` against that submodule.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe v v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ u

namespace PresheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D]
  {F : C ⥤ D} {R : Dᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}} {S : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}} (φ : S ⟶ F.op ⋙ R)
  {P : PresheafOfModules.{v} S} {Q : PresheafOfModules.{v} R}
  (ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward.{v} φ).obj Q)

/-! ### The generators over an object in the image of `F` -/

/-- **The naturality of `ψ`, read on its bundled semilinear components**: the value of `ψ` at a
restricted section over `Y` is the restriction along `F(t)` of its value over `X`.  This is
`PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply` with both sides spelled through
`PresheafOfModules.appₛₗ` and `PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ`, which is the spelling the
generating set of `PresheafOfModules.generatedSubmodule` uses. -/
theorem appₛₗ_restrictₛₗ {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (t : X ⟶ Y) (s : P.obj X) :
    appₛₗ φ ψ Y (P.restrictₛₗ t s) = Q.restrictₛₗ (F.op.map t) (appₛₗ φ ψ X s) := by
  rw [appₛₗ_apply, appₛₗ_apply]
  exact naturality_apply ψ t s

/-- **Over an object in the image of a full functor of sites, every generator of the image of the
transpose is already a value of `ψ`.**  A generator over `F(X₀)` is the restriction along some
morphism `F(X₀) ⟶ F(X)` of a value of `ψ` over `X`; fullness writes that morphism as `F(k)`, and
the naturality of `ψ` turns the restriction along `F(k)` of a value of `ψ` into a value of `ψ`
over `X₀`.

Fullness cannot be dropped: for an arbitrary `F` the morphism `F(X₀) ⟶ F(X)` need not come from
`C`, and then the restriction is only a section of `Q` over `F(X₀)` with no reason to be a value
of `ψ` there. -/
theorem pushforwardGenerators_subset_range_appₛₗ [F.Full] (X₀ : Cᵒᵖ) :
    pushforwardGenerators φ ψ (op (F.obj X₀.unop)) ⊆ Set.range (appₛₗ φ ψ X₀) := by
  rintro y ⟨X, h, s, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k : X ⟶ X₀, F.op.map k = h :=
    ⟨(F.preimage h.unop).op, by
      rw [Functor.op_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op, Functor.map_preimage, Quiver.Hom.op_unop]⟩
  exact ⟨P.restrictₛₗ k s, appₛₗ_restrictₛₗ φ ψ k s⟩

/-! ### The image of the transpose over an object in the image of `F` -/

variable [(pushforward.{v} φ).IsRightAdjoint]

/-- **The image of the transpose `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)` is exactly the image of `ψ` over `X₀`**, for a
full functor of sites `F` and a `φ.app X₀` surjective on sections.

`PresheafOfModules.range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule` gives the image of `ψ^♯` as the
`R(F X₀)`-submodule generated by the restrictions of the image of `ψ`; by
`pushforwardGenerators_subset_range_appₛₗ` those generators lie in the image of `ψ` over `X₀`, and
by the surjectivity of `φ.app X₀` that image is already an `R(F X₀)`-submodule, so the span adds
nothing.  This is the collapse that the generation half alone does not give, and it is the step
the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JN] performs when it calls the surjectivity of `c_f` and of the
`f`-map equivalent. -/
theorem range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_range_appₛₗ [F.Full] {X₀ : Cᵒᵖ}
    (hφ : Function.Surjective (φ.app X₀).hom) :
    Set.range ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app
        (op (F.obj X₀.unop))).hom = Set.range (appₛₗ φ ψ X₀) := by
  have : RingHomSurjective (φ.app X₀).hom := ⟨hφ⟩
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ ?_
  · have hgen := range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_generatedSubmodule φ ψ (op (F.obj X₀.unop))
    have hle : (generatedSubmodule φ ψ).obj (op (F.obj X₀.unop)) ≤
        LinearMap.range (appₛₗ φ ψ X₀) :=
      Submodule.span_le.2 (pushforwardGenerators_subset_range_appₛₗ φ ψ X₀)
    rintro y ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact hle (hgen.le ⟨x, rfl⟩)
  · rintro y ⟨s, rfl⟩
    exact appₛₗ_mem_range_homEquivSymm_app φ ψ X₀ s

/-- **Every value of the transpose `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)` is a value of `ψ` over `X₀`**, the element
form of `range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_range_appₛₗ`. -/
theorem exists_appₛₗ_eq_homEquivSymm_app [F.Full] {X₀ : Cᵒᵖ}
    (hφ : Function.Surjective (φ.app X₀).hom)
    (t : ((pullback.{v} φ).obj P).obj (op (F.obj X₀.unop))) :
    ∃ s : P.obj X₀, appₛₗ φ ψ X₀ s =
      ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app
        (op (F.obj X₀.unop))).hom t := by
  exact (range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_range_appₛₗ φ ψ hφ).subset (Set.mem_range_self t)

/-! ### The two surjectivities are equivalent -/

/-- **A surjective transpose forces the map it transposes to be surjective.**  If `F` is full,
`φ.app X₀` is surjective on sections and `ψ^♯` is surjective on sections over `F(X₀)`, then `ψ` is
surjective on sections over `X₀`.

This is the implication "surjectivity of `c_f` gives surjectivity of the `f`-map" of
[Stacks, Tag 07JN], for an arbitrary full functor of sites and presheaves of not necessarily
commutative rings. -/
theorem surjective_appₛₗ_of_surjective_homEquivSymm_app [F.Full] {X₀ : Cᵒᵖ}
    (hφ : Function.Surjective (φ.app X₀).hom)
    (hc : Function.Surjective
      ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app
        (op (F.obj X₀.unop))).hom) :
    Function.Surjective (appₛₗ φ ψ X₀) := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hc y
  exact exists_appₛₗ_eq_homEquivSymm_app φ ψ hφ t

/-- **Conversely, a surjective `ψ` has a surjective transpose**, and this needs no hypothesis at
all: every value of `ψ` over `X₀` is a value of `ψ^♯` over `F(X₀)`, by
`PresheafOfModules.appₛₗ_mem_range_homEquivSymm_app`. -/
theorem surjective_homEquivSymm_app_of_surjective_appₛₗ {X₀ : Cᵒᵖ}
    (hψ : Function.Surjective (appₛₗ φ ψ X₀)) :
    Function.Surjective
      ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ).app
        (op (F.obj X₀.unop))).hom := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hψ y
  exact appₛₗ_mem_range_homEquivSymm_app φ ψ X₀ s

/-! ### The local form -/

/-- **A locally surjective transpose forces the map it transposes to be locally surjective.**  Let
`J` be a Grothendieck topology on `C` and `K` one on `D`, let `F` be full and cocontinuous for the
pair, and let `φ` be surjective on sections over every object.  If the transpose
`ψ^♯ : (pullback φ).obj P ⟶ Q` is `K`-locally surjective then `ψ : P ⟶ (pushforward φ).obj Q` is
`J`-locally surjective.

Cocontinuity is what crosses the two sites: it says exactly that the `F`-pullback of a `K`-covering
sieve on `F(U)` is a `J`-covering sieve on `U`, and the sieve so obtained from the image sieve of
`ψ^♯` consists of morphisms `k : V ⟶ U` for which the section restricted to `F(V)` is a value of
`ψ^♯` there, hence by `range_homEquivSymm_app_eq_range_appₛₗ` a value of `ψ` over `V`. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_homEquivSymm [F.Full]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (K : GrothendieckTopology D) [F.IsCocontinuous J K]
    (hφ : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Function.Surjective (φ.app X).hom)
    (hc : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective K ((toPresheaf R).map
      ((((pullbackPushforwardAdjunction.{v} φ).homEquiv P Q).symm ψ)))) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J ((toPresheaf S).map ψ) where
  imageSieve_mem {U} s := by
    refine J.superset_covering ?_ (F.cover_lift J K
      (hc.imageSieve_mem (U := F.obj U) s))
    rintro V k ⟨t, ht⟩
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_appₛₗ_eq_homEquivSymm_app φ ψ (hφ (op V)) t
    exact ⟨n, hn.trans ht⟩

end PresheafOfModules
